  "plan": {
    "goal": "Recapitulate venular wall shear stress at 1 dyn/cm² (0.1 Pa) in a microvascular channel seeded with endothelial cells.",
    "rationale": "Venular shear sits at the low end of the microvascular range. HUVEC physiological shear is 0.1–1.0 Pa (registry), so 0.1 Pa (1 dyn/cm²) is the lower bound and a defensible venular target. A 400×100 µm channel at 4 µL/min yields 0.1 Pa wall shear (flow_rate_for_shear_stress). Reynolds number 0.27 confirms laminar flow; pressure drop 40 Pa is negligible for a syringe pump; residence time 12 s. HUVEC seeded at 1.5e4 cells/cm² (mid-range of 1e4–2e4) over the 0.08 cm² channel floor gives ~1200 cells.",
